# Workflow orchestration

This rule binds the kit's commands, agents, skills, and hooks into one lifecycle. Each phase command holds its own step list; this rule holds what applies to all of them.

Read `docs/agents-v0/project-profile.md` in the target repo for build/test commands, the Layout directory profile, and brownfield baseline exceptions before Build or Maintain. Profiles (`service`, `ui`, `app`) are defined in `project-delivery-core.mdc`. A filled Profile row or filled root rows win; when those rows are still placeholders, use the profile that matches the files on disk.

## Lifecycle

```mermaid
flowchart LR
  roadmap[Roadmap] -->|gate| arch[Architecture]
  arch -->|gate| plan[Plan program]
  plan -->|gate| intake
  intake[Intake] -->|gate| design[Design]
  design -->|gate| build[Build]
  build -->|gate| verify[Verify]
  verify -->|gate| release[Release]
  maintain[Maintain] --> verify
```

Phases: **Intake → Design → Build → Verify → Release**, with **Maintain** feeding back into Verify. A new program of more than one story starts with **Roadmap** (`/v0-roadmap`), then **Architecture** (`/v0-architecture`), then **Plan** (`/v0-plan`). A named ticket, and a milestone that already has an `Approved` `plan` row, start at Intake. P0-A starts at Build. Commands: `/v0-roadmap`, `/v0-architecture`, `/v0-plan`, `/v0-intake`, `/v0-design`, `/v0-build`, `/v0-verify`, `/v0-maintain`, `/v0-release`, `/v0-onboard`, `/v0-status`, `/v0-triage`, or `/v0-deliver`. `/v0-local-release` is optional after Verify. `/v0-export` and `/v0-deck` are not phases. Resume file: `docs/agents-v0/requirements/<feature>.state.json` (`sh .agents-v0/scripts/sync-feature-state.sh`). The full map is `docs/agents-v0/agents-v0-kit.md`.

## Roadmap

Discovery stays outside the kit, in any file under the repo root. `/v0-roadmap <path>` (`program-roadmap`) reads only that file and writes `docs/agents-v0/roadmap/<program>.md` with `Discovery:` set to the path. It does not copy the file. A missing path or a placeholder heading stops. The `roadmap` row (`.agents-v0/ci/check-approvals.sh <roadmap> roadmap`) covers the sequence. The discovery file has no kit approval row.

### Roadmap gate
Now, Next, and Later are in-scope items copied from the discovery file. A discovery line `Stack preference:` is copied onto the roadmap as written and does not select the pack. Stop for explicit user approval before Architecture.

## Architecture

`/v0-architecture` (`program-architecture`) runs after the `roadmap` row and before any backlog. Skip list: P0-A, a named ticket, and Maintain or Trivial. It writes the C4-through-operations pack and `docs/agents-v0/design/system/arc-record.md`. It does not write stories. One approval records the `architecture` row and names that ARC file. An `arc` row is a later amendment that supersedes the accepted ADR. Plan waits for the `architecture` row and a complete pack for the profile `Pack` cell (`pack.json`, `rules/*.mdc`, `implement-service`, `implement-bff`, and a UI manifest when `ui` names an id).

## Program planning

`/v0-plan` turns an approved roadmap and that architecture pack into milestone manifests before any `/v0-intake`. It does not rewrite the pack. `program-planner` follows `program-planning` and writes `docs/agents-v0/milestones/`, including `docs/agents-v0/milestones/plan.md` (milestone table and story flowchart). A program has no state file. Its approval is a `plan` row (`.agents-v0/ci/check-approvals.sh <manifest> plan`). P0-A alone needs no roadmap and no architecture pack. Any other program waits for the `roadmap` row and the `architecture` row. Each manifest records `Roadmap:` and `Architecture:`; `.agents-v0/ci/check-milestone.sh` checks them.

### Plan gate
Every story fits a context already on the approved context map; story-ID dependencies have no cycle; Surface and Size on each row; one surface and at most eight criteria, including the negative; an integration story for each pair of contexts that call each other; every story goal taken from the roadmap; the `plan` row after explicit user approval. `.agents-v0/ci/check-milestone.sh` fails a story with a `build` approval while a story it depends on has no `verify` approval (`MILESTONE_ORDER=0` turns that off).

## Phase resume

The state file separates the last approval from the phase in flight. `sh .agents-v0/scripts/sync-feature-state.sh` derives `lastApprovedPhase` from `Approved` rows. It never writes an approval.

| Field | Meaning |
|-------|---------|
| `lastApprovedPhase` | Last `Approved` row. Empty when none are approved. |
| `activePhase` | Phase whose command was started: `intake`, `design`, `build`, `verify`, `release`, or `maintain`. |
| `activeStatus` | `in_progress`, `awaiting_approval`, or `blocked`. |
| `blockedReason` | One line, only when `activeStatus` is `blocked`. |

Once `docs/agents-v0/requirements/<feature>.md` exists, the phase command runs `sh .agents-v0/scripts/sync-feature-state.sh <artifact> --active-phase <phase> --status in_progress` and continues from files already on disk; it does not recreate them. A red baseline, a spent attempt budget, or a missing prerequisite re-runs it with `--status blocked --reason "<one line>"` and stops. A phase ready for the user re-runs it with `--status awaiting_approval` and stops. Do not add an `Approved` row until the user approves.

`/v0-status` reads that file. `in_progress` or `blocked`: the next command is the same phase again. `awaiting_approval`: ask for approval and do not start the next phase. No active phase: name the next command from `lastApprovedPhase`. A roadmap with no `architecture` row names `/v0-architecture`. An architecture row with no `plan` row names `/v0-plan`. Also report `roadmap`, `architecture`, and `plan`. Report `arc` when `Material: yes`. Do not report `/v0-export` or `/v0-deck`.

## Parallel features

Each feature has its own `docs/agents-v0/requirements/<feature>.md`, `docs/agents-v0/requirements/<feature>.state.json`, `docs/agents-v0/design/<feature>/`, `docs/agents-v0/build/<feature>/`, and `docs/agents-v0/verify/<feature>/`. Phases of different features may proceed in one checkout only when they do not write the same shared file.

**Worktree per feature (preferred).** Run each in-flight feature in its own worktree and branch: `sh .agents-v0/scripts/feature-worktree.sh <feature>` (one explicit user authorization per feature; hooks ask). `git status` is then per feature, and catalog edits meet in the merge request (`openapi/<service>-v1.yaml` with `Service roots`). The stop conditions below apply in a shared checkout.

Shared files: `docs/agents-v0/project-profile.md`, the OpenAPI catalog (`openapi/api-v1.yaml` unless the profile names another file), `docs/agents-v0/architecture.md`, `docs/agents-v0/network.md`, `docs/agents-v0/milestones/plan.md`, `README.md`, and build or CI files (`pom.xml`, `*.csproj`, `go.mod`, `pyproject.toml`, `package.json`, `.gitlab-ci.yml`, `.gitlab/`). Ordinary feature work does not rewrite `docs/agents-v0/project-profile.md`. A feature contract draft under `docs/agents-v0/design/<feature>/` is not shared: Design writes the draft; Build merges the approved draft into the catalog.

Intake and Design for a second feature may write only that feature's requirements, state, and `docs/agents-v0/design/<feature>/` paths. Stop before editing a shared file when `git status` shows it is already modified, or when another feature's state file has `activeStatus` `in_progress`, `awaiting_approval`, or `blocked` for a phase that writes that file.

Before `/v0-build`, `/v0-verify`, `/v0-release`, or `/v0-maintain`, stop if `git status` shows another feature's code or a shared-file edit that is not this feature's approved diff. Report the paths and do not start the phase on that tree. Creating a branch needs explicit user authorization.

`/v0-status` and phase commands use the feature name the user gives. When none is named, list the state files and ask; do not assume the newest `*.state.json`.

**Milestone programs:** `docs/agents-v0/milestones/<milestone>.md` manifests group user stories. Each story runs the gated chain with approvals in its own feature artifact (`Milestone:` / `Story:` traceability). Milestone go/no-go is the `milestone` row in the manifest's `Delivery approvals` table, verified by `.agents-v0/ci/check-approvals.sh` + `.agents-v0/ci/check-milestone.sh`. A P4 manifest naming `docs/agents-v0/design/system/slo-evidence.md` also requires that file at `verify` and `release`. Record each story from its own state file; do not merge those checkouts.

## Change tiers

Pick the lightest tier that fits; record the tier in the handoff artifact.

| Tier | When | Path |
|------|------|------|
| **Trivial** | Docs-only or version-only dependency bump, when `.agents-v0/ci/classify-change.sh` says eligible and a person confirms | `/v0-triage` → `/v0-maintain` → abbreviated Verify (`/v0-verify`) |
| **Standard** | Feature or bugfix touching application code | Full Intake → Design (when contracts/UI change) → Build → Verify → Release |
| **Major** | New service, auth model, or cross-cutting architecture | Standard + ADR + threat-model notes in Design that name the applicable VAPT findings (always-on F4, F8, F9, F10, plus any regression finding the change touches); milestone manifest row |

A fix, CVE patch, upgrade, or hotfix is recorded in `docs/agents-v0/maintain/<id>/note.md` (`Maintain-Note:` in the MR) with `Tier: trivial | standard | emergency`; trivial and emergency need a person's confirmation. Emergency may merge before Verify and owes it by `Follow-up verify due`. A maintenance change never borrows a feature artifact.

## Helper agents

Phase agents do not launch helper agents (`explore-researcher`, `schema-author`, `debug-investigator`, `docs-author`). A known `/api/v1` contract launches `schema-author` in the same turn with no brief. Any other helper is a brief the phase agent writes and returns; the main session launches it once and passes `return:` back. Repeating the same `ask` is a loop: stop. Delete the brief once the result is back.

A brief holds `helper:` (agent name), `outputs:` (files to write), `return:` (fields to return), and `ask:` (one paragraph naming the files and rules).

| Phase | Brief |
|-------|--------|
| Onboard | `docs/agents-v0/onboarding/<module>.helper-brief.md` |
| Plan | `docs/agents-v0/design/system/<program>.helper-brief.md` |
| Intake | `docs/agents-v0/requirements/<feature>.helper-brief.md` |
| Design | `docs/agents-v0/design/<feature>/helper-brief.md` |
| Verify | `docs/agents-v0/verify/<feature>/helper-brief.md` |
| Maintain | `docs/agents-v0/maintain/<feature>/helper-brief.md` |

## Phase result

When a phase reaches `awaiting_approval` or `blocked`, write `docs/agents-v0/requirements/<feature>.phase-result.md` before stopping, with `phase`, `status` (`awaiting_approval` or `blocked`), `artifacts` (paths), and `blockers` (one per line). Intake also copies `user_story`, `ac_count`, `negative_count`, `regulations`, and `open_questions`. The next phase agent reads that file and the requirements artifact. Overwrite it when the phase changes (per-feature, not shared).

## Command results

Each verify attempt appends a card (Command, Exit, Attempt, Failing test, Location `file:line`) to `docs/agents-v0/build/<feature>/build-report.md`. Raw logs stay in CI or `build-output.txt`; the next attempt must not read `build-output.txt`.

## Phase attempt budget

A phase has a total budget of failed cards (Exit not 0): the `Phase attempt budget` row in `docs/agents-v0/project-profile.md` (default 8). Before each new attempt run `sh .agents-v0/scripts/check-attempt-budget.sh docs/agents-v0/build/<feature>/build-report.md`. On exit 1, record `blocked` with reason `attempt budget exhausted`, write the phase result, and stop. Only the user raises the budget in the profile row.

## Conduct model (from `ai-agent-conduct.mdc`)

Every phase follows **Reconnaissance → Plan → Execute → Verify → Report**.

## Phase → agent → skill → handoff artifact

| Phase | Command | Lead agent | Skill(s) | Handoff artifact |
|-------|---------|-----------|----------|------------------|
| Roadmap (program) | `/v0-roadmap` | `program-planner` | `program-roadmap` | `docs/agents-v0/roadmap/<program>.md` (`roadmap` row, `Discovery:` path) |
| Architecture (program) | `/v0-architecture` | `solution-architect` | `program-architecture` | `docs/agents-v0/architecture.md` (`architecture` row names the ARC file), before any story |
| Plan (program) | `/v0-plan` | `program-planner` | `program-planning` | `docs/agents-v0/milestones/plan.md` and `docs/agents-v0/milestones/<milestone>.md` (`plan` row; Surface and Size on each story). Reads the architecture pack |
| Intake | `/v0-intake` | `requirements-analyst` | `spec-intake` | `docs/agents-v0/requirements/<feature>.md` (Gherkin `AC-*`, `Kind`, NFRs, regulations, `Delivery approvals`) |
| Design | `/v0-design` | `solution-architect`, `ux-designer` | `contract-first-design`, `ux-design` | OpenAPI + events, ADR, diagrams, UX spec, mockups; `docs/agents-v0/design/system/arc-record.md` when `Material: yes` |
| Build | `/v0-build` | `backend-engineer` / `bff-engineer` / `frontend-engineer` | `implement-*` | Code + migrations + tests; `docs/agents-v0/build/<feature>/` evidence |
| Verify | `/v0-verify` | `test-engineer`, then `security-reviewer` and `code-reviewer` together | `quality-gate`, `vapt-review`, `pr-review` | `docs/agents-v0/verify/<feature>/` reports |
| Maintain | `/v0-maintain` | `maintenance-engineer` | `bugfix-triage`, `dependency-upgrade`, `doc-sync`, `characterization-tests`, `migration-safety` | Fix + docs; approval to re-enter Verify |
| Release | `/v0-release` | `release-manager` | `release-pr` | Merge request ready; completion after human merge |

**Release semantics:** Merge-request readiness (docs, VAPT sign-off, CI green) is **not** completion; Release completes only after an authorized human merge and green CI. Opening the merge request, commits, and pushes each need explicit user approval; agents must not bypass the hook prompts.

## Gates

A phase is **not complete** until its gate passes. Stop where that phase command says to stop.

**Approval recording:** record gate decision, approver, date, evidence paths, and N/A reasons in the phase handoff artifact's `Delivery approvals` table (`| Phase | Artifacts | Approver | Decision | Date |`). Never infer approval. Decision must be an explicit positive token (`Approved`; CI accepts `approved` / `yes` / `pass`). Include `commit: <sha>` in Build/Verify artifact columns when evidence is produced.

**Batch approval.** Only Intake and Design gates may be approved for several stories in one message when the user names every story (`Approved: Design for P2-A, P2-B`). Each named story must be Standard tier with no security-review trigger, no open question, and no `Vertical slice: yes`; any other story is approved alone. Each story's artifact still gets its own row (`orchestrator` holds the steps). Build, Verify, and Release are always per story.

**Brownfield baseline:** if `docs/agents-v0/project-profile.md` documents `known_failures` or a ratchet plan, Build may proceed only when the profile allows it and new failures are not introduced.

### Intake gate
- User story recorded as `As a [role], I want [goal], so that [benefit].`
- Acceptance criteria (`### AC-1` …) follow `spec-intake`. `.agents-v0/ci/check-intake.sh` must pass: `Kind`, the `Then`, one `negative` or `edge` (or `Negatives: N/A` with no security trigger), preconditions, a desk check, NFRs, and regulations. Open questions are `none`. `Material: yes` or `no`. P0-A skips the check.
- **Story size.** One primary surface (`Surfaces: backend`, `bff`, or `frontend`), one bounded context, at most eight acceptance criteria (`AC-1` through `AC-8`), including the negative. A larger story stops on `## Proposed split` (`spec-intake`). `Vertical slice: yes` only when the user asks for one journey across surfaces.
- UI-affecting: UX requirements per `ux-design.mdc`.

### Design gate
- `design.md` at `docs/agents-v0/design/<feature>/`, plus a `/api/v1` draft when the story adds one (otherwise `N/A: no /api/v1 operation`). Failure modes name every negative and edge `AC-*`. Stop at Design for an OpenAPI draft, an AsyncAPI or `events/` contract, a UX spec, a public route other than `/health`, `/ready`, or `/live`, or `Material: yes` (`design-reviewer` writes `review.md`). Otherwise pin without `review.md` and write the Design row with the Build approval. The pin includes `asyncapi.yaml` and the cited ADR. A later change is an amendment; a changed decision supersedes the ADR. The org catalog stays unchanged. UX spec and mockups when UI-affecting (`ux-design.mdc`). P0-A skips Intake and Design (Build copies the milestone story and AC-1 through AC-4, writes that N/A design, and pins it).
- `Material: yes` writes or cites `docs/agents-v0/design/system/arc-record.md` (two options, a recommendation, SLO targets in `nfr-slo.md`, and a structural fitness-function table). The `arc` row is separate from Design (`.agents-v0/ci/check-arc.sh`). P4 measures or waives SLO rows in `slo-evidence.md`.
- Non-trivial security: brief threat-model notes (assets, trust boundaries, top risks) naming applicable VAPT findings in `security-baseline.mdc` (always-on F4, F8, F9, F10).

### Build gate
- **Baseline green** before first edit, unless `/v0-build` skips a checkout that is already the default branch tip; otherwise the profile verify command. Stop on a pre-existing failure unless the profile allows it.
- **Build plan** at `docs/agents-v0/build/<feature>/plan.md` before the first implementation edit: one row per approved `AC-*` (AC, Status `pending`/`done`/`blocked`, Test). A green unit sets its row to `done` and names the test. Do not add, delete, or rewrite AC rows.
- **Red–green loop** on the profile's **fast** verify cell (real command, not a placeholder). Capture the red report with `check-build-plan.sh <feature> --record-red` before green. A done row needs a red card; when `red-tests.json` exists, the test name must be in it. Gate: full verify once (coverage/static/CVE). Second red for the same test → `failure-brief.md` + `check-failure-brief.sh` before attempt three; third red stops. Do not read `build-output.txt` again. ≤ 3 fixes per failure.
- When `docs/agents-v0/design/<feature>/openapi.yaml` exists, merge that approved draft into the org catalog before other implementation edits. Stop when the catalog is already modified by another feature. A story with no draft records N/A in the build report.
- Quality tooling wired from the pack. Red–green tests for new behavior; VAPT-required tests in the same diff when applicable.
- Contract conformance and the pack layer check where wired; methods ≤ 30 lines; auth+authz; correlation/tracing; DTOs only; pack migrations; no secrets. A migration or SQL diff with `DIFF_BASE` set must hit the profile database; H2 does not count. No down script is legal with a rollback note (`migration-safety`).
- UX spec implemented for UI changes: component defaults, layout matching the approved mockups, API client only for operations named on those rows.
- **Build evidence** under `docs/agents-v0/build/<feature>/` (`build-report.md` with `commit:` line; optional `build-output.txt` — prefer CI artifacts for raw logs).

### Verify gate
- `test-engineer` finishes first and may change tests. Then `security-reviewer` and `code-reviewer` run together. Each writes only its own report (`vapt-checklist.md`, `review-notes.md`). Wait for both, including when one finds a Critical item. Gather one Critical list into `docs/agents-v0/requirements/<feature>.phase-result.md`, then route back to Build or Maintain.
- Quality, security (VAPT), UX (axe-core + UX AC tests), code review — no Critical findings.
- Numbers come from machine output. `check-gate-metrics.sh` fails zero tests, failures, changed lines under 80% when `DIFF_BASE` is set, an H2-only schema diff, a missed `mutation_ratchet`, and unsuppressed HIGH/CRITICAL CVEs. Report check: 80% backend / 70% frontend. `check-event-schemas.sh` rejects non-additive events. Reports quote those results; they do not replace them.
- Integration stories, vertical slices, P2 journeys, and P4 stories also persist `docs/agents-v0/verify/<feature>/e2e-report.md` (`e2e-perf-testing`).
- The P4 SLO story writes `docs/agents-v0/design/system/slo-evidence.md` (`slo-evidence`): each filled NFR/SLO row is `measured` (command plus an output file) or `waiver` (reason, approver, date).
- Evidence under `docs/agents-v0/verify/<feature>/` with `commit:` in each report header; tests added during Verify are committed before stamping, so every report names the same commit.
- N/A only with a recorded reason. An applicable miss on an always-on VAPT finding (F4, F8, F9, F10) is Critical. HIGH and MEDIUM regression findings block merge when the diff touches that surface. LOW regression findings block only when the diff makes the issue exploitable.

### Release gate
- README and sequence diagrams synced; `architecture.md` and `network.md` stay a docs-only follow-up; MR/PR template + VAPT sign-off; CI green; `release` row (Approver = the GitLab username that approves the MR) recorded on the MR branch before merge.
- On GitLab, after the MR is approved, run the manual `delivery-approval` job. It matches that approver to an Approved release or verify row. `GITLAB_TOKEN` is a masked project access token with `read_api` scope, limited to the `delivery-approval` environment.
- Completion = authorized human merge; that merge (reviews, checks, merge commit) is the record — no follow-up commit to record it.
- When `docs/agents-v0/project-profile.md` has a **Deploy** table, `release-deploy` runs after the merge: one authorization, deploy command, smoke check (optional SLO probe against `nfr-slo.md`), and rollback per environment. A failed smoke or probe rolls back and stops. Records go in a docs-only follow-up MR, never a commit to the default branch.

## Approval stops

`/v0-deliver` stops where the phase command says to stop. On Critical findings, route to Build/Maintain and re-enter Verify.

## Documentation

`/v0-export` and `/v0-deck` write derived files from approved records. They add no `Approved` row. `/v0-deliver` does not call them. A missing CSV or deck does not block a phase. Detail is in those commands.

## Rule precedence

If project files contradict a rule, **the repository wins**. Record approved per-repo exceptions in `docs/agents-v0/project-profile.md` and ADRs. Change org-wide kit rules only in `core/common/rules/*.mdc`, and pack rules in `core/<pack>/rules/`.
